## 1. Introduction to Dynatrace

### What is Dynatrace?
Dynatrace is an AI-powered, full-stack observability and application performance management (APM) platform. It automatically discovers, monitors, and analyzes the entire technology stack — from applications and microservices to infrastructure and user experience — using a single agent (OneAgent) and AI engine (Davis AI).

### Why Dynatrace?
- **Automatic discovery**: OneAgent auto-discovers all processes, services, and dependencies — no manual configuration needed.
- **AI-powered root cause analysis**: Davis AI correlates billions of data points to pinpoint the exact root cause of problems.
- **Full-stack monitoring**: From browser/mobile → application → service → process → host → network → cloud infrastructure.
- **Real User Monitoring (RUM)**: Captures every real user session — not samples.
- **Code-level visibility**: Provides method-level response time breakdowns, exceptions, and database call analysis.
- **Cloud-native support**: Kubernetes, Docker, AWS, Azure, GCP, OpenShift native integration.

### Dynatrace vs Traditional APM Tools
| Feature | Dynatrace | Traditional APM |
|---------|-----------|-----------------|
| Discovery | Automatic (OneAgent) | Manual agent config per app |
| AI/Root Cause | Davis AI (automatic) | Rule-based alerts, manual analysis |
| Full Stack | Single platform | Multiple tools stitched together |
| Scalability | Handles millions of entities | Often limited |
| Deployment | Single agent for everything | Different agents per technology |
| Cloud-Native | Built for K8s, serverless | Bolted-on support |

### Key Use Cases
- **Application Performance Management (APM)**: Monitor application health, response times, error rates, throughput.
- **Infrastructure Monitoring**: CPU, memory, disk, network across hosts, VMs, containers.
- **Digital Experience Monitoring (DEM)**: Real User Monitoring (RUM), Synthetic Monitoring, Session Replay.
- **Cloud & Kubernetes Monitoring**: Full visibility into K8s clusters, pods, nodes, namespaces.
- **AIOps**: Automated problem detection, root cause analysis, and alerting via Davis AI.
- **Business Analytics**: Map technical metrics to business KPIs (revenue, conversions, etc.).
- **Log Management & Analytics**: Ingest, search, and analyze logs alongside metrics and traces.
- **Security**: Runtime Application Self-Protection (RASP), vulnerability detection.

