## 2. Dynatrace Architecture

### Core Components

#### 1. OneAgent
- A single agent installed on each monitored host.
- Automatically discovers all running processes, services, and applications.
- Injects into application processes to capture code-level data (method calls, SQL queries, exceptions).
- Captures metrics, traces, logs, and real user data.
- Communicates with Dynatrace Cluster/SaaS via encrypted HTTPS.
- Auto-updates without restarts (in most cases).
- Supports: Java, .NET, Node.js, PHP, Go, Python, C/C++, and more.

#### 2. ActiveGate
- An optional proxy/gateway between OneAgents and the Dynatrace server.
- **Use cases:**
  - Route OneAgent traffic through a single point (firewall-friendly).
  - Monitor remote technologies (VMware, databases, cloud APIs) that don't run OneAgent.
  - Perform synthetic monitoring from specific locations.
  - Act as a cluster node for Dynatrace Managed.

**Types of ActiveGate:**
| Type | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **Environment ActiveGate** | Routes OneAgent data, runs remote plugins, synthetic monitors |
| **Cluster ActiveGate** | Specific to Dynatrace Managed; handles cluster operations |

#### 3. Dynatrace Server (Backend)
- **Dynatrace SaaS**: Hosted by Dynatrace in the cloud. No infrastructure management needed.
- **Dynatrace Managed**: Self-hosted on your own infrastructure. Full control over data residency.

The server stores all collected data, runs Davis AI analysis, serves the web UI, and provides APIs.

#### 4. Davis AI Engine
- The artificial intelligence engine at the core of Dynatrace.
- Continuously analyzes billions of dependencies and data points.
- **Deterministic AI**: Uses topology, transactional data, and causation — not just correlation.
- Automatically detects problems, identifies root causes, and determines business impact.
- Requires no training, no rules, no thresholds — works out of the box.

### Architecture Diagram (Conceptual)
```
Users (Browser/Mobile)
        │
        ▼
┌─── Real User Monitoring (JavaScript agent) ───┐
│                                                 │
▼                                                 ▼
Application Servers ◄── OneAgent ──► ActiveGate ──► Dynatrace Server (SaaS/Managed)
     │                                                      │
     ├── Databases                                     Davis AI Engine
     ├── Message Queues                                     │
     ├── Cloud Services                              Smartscape Topology
     └── Kubernetes/Docker                                  │
                                                      Web UI / API
```

### Communication & Ports
| Port | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| 443 | OneAgent → Dynatrace SaaS (HTTPS) |
| 443 | OneAgent → ActiveGate (HTTPS) |
| 9999 | OneAgent communication port (local) |
| 8021 | ActiveGate internal communication |
| 9200 | Dynatrace Managed — Elasticsearch (internal) |
| 8019 | Dynatrace Managed — Cluster communication |

