## 3. Dynatrace Deployment & Installation

### 3.1 OneAgent Installation

#### Linux
```bash
# Download and run the installer (from Dynatrace UI: Deploy → Start Installation)
wget -O Dynatrace-OneAgent.sh "https://<your-environment>.live.dynatrace.com/api/v1/deployment/installer/agent/unix/default/latest?Api-Token=<TOKEN>&arch=x86&flavor=default"
chmod +x Dynatrace-OneAgent.sh
sudo /bin/sh Dynatrace-OneAgent.sh --set-app-log-content-access=true

# Verify installation
sudo systemctl status oneagent
```

#### Windows
```powershell
# Download the MSI installer from Dynatrace UI
# Run the installer
msiexec /i Dynatrace-OneAgent.msi

# Or via PowerShell
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://<env>.live.dynatrace.com/api/v1/deployment/installer/agent/windows/default/latest?Api-Token=<TOKEN>" -OutFile Dynatrace-OneAgent.exe
.\Dynatrace-OneAgent.exe
```

#### Docker / Container
```dockerfile
# Method 1: Add to Dockerfile
COPY Dynatrace-OneAgent.sh /tmp/
RUN /bin/sh /tmp/Dynatrace-OneAgent.sh --set-app-log-content-access=true

# Method 2: Kubernetes Operator (recommended)
# Install via Dynatrace Operator (Helm or YAML)
```

#### Kubernetes (Dynatrace Operator)
```bash
# Install Dynatrace Operator via Helm
helm repo add dynatrace https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dynatrace/dynatrace-operator/main/config/helm/repos/stable
helm install dynatrace-operator dynatrace/dynatrace-operator \
  --namespace dynatrace \
  --create-namespace

# Create DynaKube custom resource
kubectl apply -f dynakube.yaml
```

```yaml
# dynakube.yaml
apiVersion: dynatrace.com/v1beta1
kind: DynaKube
metadata:
  name: dynakube
  namespace: dynatrace
spec:
  apiUrl: https://<environment-id>.live.dynatrace.com/api
  tokens: dynakube     # Secret name containing API and PaaS tokens
  oneAgent:
    cloudNativeFullStack: {}   # Full monitoring for K8s
```

**Deployment Modes for Kubernetes:**
| Mode | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Cloud-Native Full Stack** | Full monitoring: infrastructure + application + code-level |
| **Classic Full Stack** | OneAgent DaemonSet on every node |
| **Application-Only** | Code-level only (no infrastructure metrics) — for PaaS/serverless |
| **Host Monitoring** | Infrastructure only (CPU, memory, disk) — no code injection |

