## 18. Security in Dynatrace

### 18.1 Runtime Application Self-Protection (RASP)
Dynatrace can detect runtime vulnerabilities:
- SQL injection attempts
- Command injection
- SSRF (Server-Side Request Forgery)
- Path traversal
- Detected in real-time from PurePath / trace data.

### 18.2 Runtime Vulnerability Analytics
- Scans libraries/dependencies used by monitored processes.
- Identifies known CVEs (Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures).
- Shows which services are affected.
- Provides CVSS scores and remediation advice.
- Continuously updated — new vulnerabilities detected as CVE databases update.

**Security overview**: Shows all vulnerabilities by severity (Critical, High, Medium, Low), affected entities, and exposure status.

### 18.3 Data Privacy
Dynatrace provides configureable data privacy controls:

- **Session Replay masking**: Mask user inputs, text content, images.
- **Do Not Track**: Respect browser DNT headers.
- **Data retention**: Configure how long data is kept.
- **Personal data masking**: Mask IP addresses, user IDs in RUM data.
- **Request attribute exclusion**: Exclude sensitive headers/parameters.
- **Log masking**: Apply masking rules to log content before storage.

